{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118729","id":3550824507,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7TpUg7","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118729","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118729.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118729.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118729","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118729/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118729/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118729/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/96e362bef2649f660834fc2bc815467d3c7ec458","number":118729,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Fix sub-emitter AT_START first emission lost after inactivity","user":{"login":"christiaanvw","id":6009570,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDk1NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6009570?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/christiaanvw","html_url":"https://github.com/christiaanvw","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christiaanvw/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christiaanvw/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christiaanvw/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christiaanvw/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christiaanvw/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christiaanvw/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christiaanvw/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christiaanvw/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christiaanvw/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Summary of changes:** Only clear the sub-emitter buffer when force_sub_emit is false.\r\n\r\n**Motivation:** [issue](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118727) - GPUParticles3D sub-emitter AT_START: first emission after inactivity does not spawns sub-particles\r\n\r\n**Related work:** N/A\r\n\r\n**Technical overview:** Only clear the sub-emitter buffer when force_sub_emit is false, indicating the sub-emitter has consumed its data. force_sub_emit is set to true by the parent, and reset to false by the sub-emitter at the start of its own _particles_process().\r\n\r\n**Testing:** Manually tested in my own game. I also created a dedicated scene consistently demonstrating this bug (see [issue](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118727)). After applying the fix the bug disappeared. Additionally confirmed with print_line debugging that force_sub_emit was indeed true when the buffer was being cleared, validating the root cause.\r\n\r\n**Discussion:** Particles are complex systems, as a first time contributor feels impossible to oversee and test all possible scenario's. However, I believe the question to be answered is: \"Why would anyone want to unconditionally clear the sub-emitter buffer when force_sub_emit is set to true?\". I couldn't think of a good reason.\r\n\r\n**Additional work:** N/A\r\n\r\n**AI disclosure:** I used Claude to explore the engine codebase. The bug discovery, analysis, and fix are my own work.\r\n\r\n- *Bugsquad edit:* This PR fixes https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118727","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":4442850752,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCNCFwA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:particles","name":"topic:particles","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"mi